agent-ops task task-b302b92c-1234-47f5-a911-d9aac716bd09: Office batch 3: prop panels with review and failure detail
intent: Clicking the five office props opens a panel: whiteboard (task and criteria), cubicle screen (changed files), QA status board (verify evidence with failure output), exec desk (review rounds and findings) and sorting table (worktree and integration steps). The data side reads review report JSON and acceptance execution artifacts read-only, with strict path patterns, re-redaction and size caps; plain-command evidence stays without output. Split into a data subtask and a panels subtask.
criteria:
- panels-integrate: In a room, clicking each of the five props (whiteboard, cubicle screen, QA status board, exec desk, sorting table) opens its panel built from the snapshot; a client test opens all five.
- literal-text: Panels render every snapshot string with textContent, never innerHTML; a client test feeds HTML-looking review findings and failure output and finds them shown literally.
  agent-ops task task-dc338759-de44-47d9-97c8-89dd922e79ad: B3 data: review reports and failure output, read safely
  intent: collect.ts adds desk.review from the newest review report JSON for the task and criterion.output from acceptance execution artifacts, plus worktree base and ahead count. Every read is pattern-checked, symlink-safe via readPrivateFile, size-capped and re-redacted.
  criteria:
  - review-summary: The newest .agent-ops/reviews/<fingerprint>.<taskId>.reports.json by createdAt becomes desk.review with status PASS/FAIL/NOT_RUN, createdAt, reason, the rounds (target, summary, findings with severity, blocking, title, details, recommendation) and whether the adversarial round refuted; a test with an older PASS and a newer FAIL report picks the FAIL.
  - failure-output: A FAIL or UNKNOWN criterion whose newest evidence has an acceptance execution artifact gets output = the redacted last 2048 bytes of its stderr and stdout; plain-command evidence and passing criteria get output null; a test covers both.
  - containment: Only artifact paths matching .agent-ops/tasks/acceptance/<64 hex>.json and review files named <64 hex>.<taskId>.reports.json inside .agent-ops/reviews are read, through readPrivateFile so symlinks are refused; a test with a forged path pointing outside and a symlinked report reads neither.
  - caps-redaction: Secrets in review text and failure output are redacted again on read, review files over 512 KiB are ignored, summaries, finding fields and recommendations are cut to fixed byte limits and at most 10 findings per round are kept; a test checks a token and the limits.
  - integration-facts: Worktree desks carry base (the base commit, first 12 hex) and ahead (the number of commits past the base); a test with a fake commit counter checks both.
  agent-ops task task-a640f22e-6f0b-4bac-a5d8-3cf827183475: B3 panels: five prop panels in the room
  intent: Prop hotspots in layout.ts; clicking a prop or pressing Enter near it opens a themed panel dialog built from the snapshot desk (task and criteria, changed files, verify evidence, review rounds, worktree and integration steps). Text only through textContent.
  criteria:
  - hotspots: layout.ts defines one hotspot per panel prop (whiteboard, cubicle screens, QA status board and bench, exec desk, sorting table), each inside its room; clicking a hotspot opens the matching panel and Enter within reach of one opens it too; a client test checks a click and an Enter.
  - task-and-diff: The whiteboard panel shows the task title, the five phases with the current one marked, the criteria as notes grouped into not verified, failed and passed, open questions and copyable commands; the screen panel lists changed files with the most recent one marked and the file, insertion and deletion totals with the branch; a client test checks both.
  - verify-and-review: The QA panel shows every criterion with its status, failure class, exit code and time, the failure output tail in a preformatted block when present, and a copyable verify command; the exec desk panel shows the review status, each round's reviewer, summary and findings, whether the re-check refuted, or 'not reviewed yet', plus a copyable review command; a client test checks both, including a missing review.
  - integration: The sorting table panel shows the worktree, branch, base and commits ahead, and the steps commit, verify, review and finish each marked done, failed or pending from the snapshot, plus a copyable worktree finish command; a client test checks a worktree with a failed verify.
